    A4 123 — reduced, not addressed, next docket.
  * THE FASTPATH PAID FOR ITSELF: it caught that nearest-spine selection by
    coordinate identity yields an EMPTY set on real data (no emitted apron
    ring vertex equals an axes_exact vertex; the owner's node sits 0.002 m
    off the line), so A4.1(i) would have shipped inert.

THE MECHANISM WORKS AND DOES NOT PAY.  Three findings, in order of weight.

1. *** THE PRECEDENCE HOLDS EXACTLY: senior nodes MOVED in A2 = 0 on all
   three airports. ***  The spec's own STOP condition is not tripped; the
   freeze covers the sweeps AND the band clamp.  Flag-off is proven
   byte-for-byte on CYXY: O4_APRON_STAGED_SOLVE=0 rebuilds body_sha
   40617f978f7a, exactly compose-v3's (twin (c) on a real airport).

2. *** A1'S BOTH-HARD RESIDUE IS ESSENTIALLY NIL, WHICH REFUTES THE
   SPEC'S OWN PREMISE. ***  Section 4 expected A1's both-hard count to be
   "the honest pin-contradiction number" and the top-20 to be the next
   round's brief.  Measured:
     CYXY  1 row,  worst 0.055 m  (runway-datum / runway-datum)
     SPJC 26 rows, worst 0.006 m  (unified:apron, terrain / terrain)
     HECA  4 rows, worst 0.446 m  (unified:junction, runway-datum both ends)
   THE PINS DO NOT CONTRADICT THE MOVEMENT-SURFACE LAW.  A1's over_cap is
   large (HECA 4309, SPJC 324, CYXY 4) while its BOTH-HARD is 4/26/1, so
   the senior law is FEASIBLE and the residue is ordinary unconverged
   projection, not a pin contradiction.  There is no pin docket to hand on.

3. *** THE STAGED SOLVE CANNOT MOVE THE NUMBER BECAUSE THE SENIOR SET IS
   ALMOST THE WHOLE APRON. ***  Interior movers vs seniors re-frozen in A2:
     CYXY 114 movers / 272 seniors      (of 33,360 nodes)
     SPJC 355 movers / 2,195 seniors    (of 63,696)
     HECA 334 movers / 1,506 seniors    (of 139,459)
   Under A2's predicates 82-86 % of the interior-pair endpoints are
   already movement surfaces, so A2 has almost nothing to move and
   precedence has almost nothing to protect.  CYXY's sidecar partition
   says the same in the large: 287 senior / 206 interior of 493 apron ring
   nodes.  A mechanism that reorders two sets cannot help when one of them
   is nearly empty.

