TWO DEFECTS THE BUILDS FOUND IN THIS ROUND'S OWN CODE, both fixed:
  * a SPLIT LAZY ENTRY killed the SPJC build at 288 s (KeyError
    'lazy_nodes'): the interior half inherited ``lazy_expand`` while the
    strip list removed its node lists.  A lazy entry is now never split.
  * the pin docket first reported the WRONG POPULATION (re-derived from
    the joint list, so it printed stage-B service_road / service_junction
    families the senior pass never enforced) and every pin source as "?"
    (invented layout attribute names).  Rows are now recorded inside the
    senior pass; sources come from the sets that actually froze the nodes.
  Neither had a surface effect: the CYXY body sha is 6c0cf4f2fd97 across
  all three code states.

WHAT THE COMPOSED LANE BOUGHT AND KEEPS: transverse is at or below the
battery on all three and best in the staged arm at HECA (95 -> 46) and
SPJC (46 -> 41); steps are gone at SPJC (37 -> 0) and near-gone at HECA
(192 -> 11); CYXY clears its bar by 51 and the service_junction spine
37.1 % row that survived apronpop AND v1 is gone from v2 onward.

TESTS.  397 passed / 2 failed across nine suites.  Both failures are
PRE-EXISTING and neither belongs to this round:
``test_the_near_miss_frontage_law_is_one_authority`` is one of the 11 the
apronpop lane measured on its matched CONTROL, and
``test_the_solve_ingests_the_family_at_BOTH_edge_set_sites`` fails on
lane/transect ALONE (verified in that worktree).  The staged solve's own
twins are 14/14 (spec section 6 (a)-(d) plus the two lazy-entry twins the
SPJC crash earned).

DOCKET (named, with sites, nothing fixed here)
  1. BLEND-CREDIT READER DRIFT (the cap-lockstep twin's find).  On ONE
     apron ring edge the bake reads the BLEND branch's 1.5 % ("an apron
     body edge near a taxiway earns the route's blended cap") while the
     census reads the plain 1.0 % body cap.  Site: the twin fixture's
     bottom ring edge, layout-local (-100,-40)-(300,-40), lat/lon
     (30.4996407,31.4989583)-(30.4996407,31.5031250).  Present with the
     interior flag ON and OFF before A2; under A2 that edge is INTERIOR,
     both readers agree at 5 %, and the drift is GONE from the shipping
     configuration — but the underlying gap is untouched and is still
     asserted on the flag-off arm so it cannot be forgotten.
  2. MEMO KEY OMITS THE INTERIOR FLAG (test-only).
     ``shape_constraints_cached`` is keyed by CONTENT (ring, role,
     ring_only, ctx); the interior-cap flag is not in the key, so an
     identical ring re-run with the flag flipped is served the first arm's
     caps.  Production reads the flag once at import so nothing ships
     wrong, but every flag-off twin through that path must use its own
     geometry.  Found in test_fan_ramp_law.
  3. THE SPJC WELD CLUSTER at (-12.021394,-77.110990) — 39 sub-5 m ring
     edges at 15-35x their cap where ways -10113/-10162/-10698/-10699 meet.
  4. HECA's 152 kept frontage rows > 5 %.
  5. broken_by_emit at 46-65 % — what A1 §8d exists to trigger.
  6. A role-LESS duplicate ring of an apron host is priced strictly while
     its host prices its interior at 5 % (one geometry, two laws).
  7. SPLP / KAFW / KDFW still have no arm under this tree.

THE QUESTION THE MEASUREMENTS PUT BACK TO THE OWNER.  No arm passes all
three airports: CYXY wants v2/v3, SPJC is ~+20 in both, HECA is best in v1
(1167) and worst in v3 (2560).  Since no violation is ever priced at 5 %,
the interior CAP is not the lever that closes HECA — what closes it is
whatever stops the interior from tilting into its movement surfaces.  That
is a different mechanism from a cap value, and it is an owner/spec call.
